#: manual/api/dual.md:1
msgid "dual API"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dual.md:5
msgid "The `dual` package owns `Dual[T]`, the dual number $a + b\\varepsilon$ with $\\varepsilon^2 = 0$, together with its arithmetic, its Luna Flow trait instances and the derivative rules of the elementary functions. Every other package of this repository re-exports or consumes this type. The mathematics behind the rules is in the [dual design](../design/dual.md)."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dual.md:11
msgid "Source: [`src/dual/dual.mbt`](../../../src/dual/dual.mbt), [`src/dual/extends.mbt`](../../../src/dual/extends.mbt) and [`src/dual/compat.mbt`](../../../src/dual/compat.mbt)."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dual.md:23
msgid "Most programs import the root package `Luna-Flow/autodiff` instead, which re-exports `Dual` as `@autodiff.Dual` (see the [autodiff API](autodiff.md)). The examples on this page use the root alias."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dual.md:27
msgid "The type"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dual.md:31
msgid "`Dual[T]` stores a primal value and a first-order tangent."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dual.md:40
msgid "The pair `(value, tangent)` represents $a + b\\varepsilon$ with $a$ = `value` and $b$ = `tangent`. When a computation starts from `Dual::variable(x)`, the tangent of every intermediate result is the derivative of that intermediate with respect to `x`. The fields are read-only outside the package; build values with the constructors below."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dual.md:46
msgid "`derive(Eq)` compares both components, so two dual numbers with the same value and different tangents are not equal. `derive(Debug)` prints the record form `{ value: …, tangent: … }`, which `debug_inspect` and `assert_eq` use."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dual.md:51
msgid "`Dual[T]` deliberately has no `Compare`, `Field`, `MulGroup`, `Inverse` or `Show` instance; see [Design decisions](../design/dual.md#design-decisions)."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dual.md:54
msgid "Construction and access"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dual.md:58
msgid "Builds $a + b\\varepsilon$ from an explicit value and tangent."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dual.md:64
msgid ""
"Use it to seed a direction other than $1$, for example a directional derivative $\\n"
"abla f(x) \\cdot v$ where each input coordinate gets the tangent $v_i$."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dual.md:70
msgid "Embeds a value with tangent zero: $c \\mapsto c + 0\\varepsilon$."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dual.md:76
msgid "Constants do not depend on the differentiation variable, so their derivative is $0$. Use it for every literal or captured value that enters a differentiated computation."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dual.md:82
msgid "Embeds the differentiation variable with tangent one: $x \\mapsto x + 1\\varepsilon$."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dual.md:91
msgid "Returns the primal component $a$."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dual.md:99
msgid "Returns the tangent component $b$."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dual.md:119
msgid "Returns the additive identity $0 + 0\\varepsilon$."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dual.md:126
msgid "This is the promoted method of the `Zero` instance."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dual.md:130
msgid "Returns the multiplicative identity $1 + 0\\varepsilon$."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dual.md:137
msgid "`one` is a constant, so its tangent is zero; it is not `Dual::variable(1)`. This is the promoted method of the `One` instance."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dual.md:142
msgid "Embeds a natural number, given as a `BigInt`, as a constant."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dual.md:149
msgid "`from_natural(n)` is `Dual::constant(FromNat::from_natural(n))`. This is the promoted method of the `FromNat` instance."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dual.md:154
msgid "Embeds an integer, given as a `BigInt`, as a constant."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dual.md:161
msgid "`from_integer(n)` is `Dual::constant(FromInteger::from_integer(n))`, the canonical map $\\mathbb Z \\to T[\\varepsilon]$. This is the promoted method of the `FromInteger` instance. To convert an `Int` or another integral type, use `@lg.lift_to(n)` from `Luna-Flow/luna-generic`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dual.md:175
